From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jason chien <3936511+jason5545@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 21:12:26 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] FEXCore, ARM64EC: adaptive per-page SMC handling (hot
 pages)

Port of steamac-dr 8035502f2 (0005) and a26b7d158 (0006) from the Linux
frontend to the Windows one (InvalidationTracker, used by ARM64EC).

With SMCChecks=mtrack every RWX guest page FEX compiled code from is
protected PAGE_EXECUTE_READ. A write faults, goes through Wine's
exception dispatch into ResetToConsistentState, and
HandleRWXAccessViolation drops every block of the page in every thread
and unprotects it; the next compile protects it again. On Wine ARM64EC
(CrossOver 27 Preview, Apple Silicon) that costs 27-37 us per write
(tools/smc-test T1), 3-4x the Linux path. MSFS 2024's four-slot
breakpoint phase writes data into pages it keeps executing; there a
round takes ~0.8 s on the Mac against 28-65 ms with hot pages on Linux.

A page that takes STEAMAC_SMC_HOT (default 8, 0 disables) write faults
within 2 s becomes hot for the rest of the process: it is no longer
write-protected, and every instruction compiled from it validates its
own guest bytes before it runs with the SMCChecks=full check.

FEXCore (same as the Linux version):
- SteamacSMC: lock-free fault counters (16384 slots, 8-way open
  addressing) and hot-page table. The clock is the generic timer
  (cntvct_el0) instead of clock_gettime; no function-local statics.
- GenerateIR: per-instruction validation on hot pages.
- CompileBlock: no disk-cached code for hot pages.
- InvalidateCodeBuffersCodeRange returns whether the range had code
  pages; new InvalidateThreadExecutableRangeCache.

Windows frontend:
- HandleRWXAccessViolation: NoteFault with CodeInvalidationMutex held,
  before the page is invalidated and unprotected.
- ProtectRWXIntervalsInternal (re-protect after a compile): leave hot
  pages writable.
- InvalidateIntervalInternalLocked: no per-thread L1/L2 walk when no
  code buffer had code in the range.
- ARM64EC InvalidateGuestCodeRange takes ThreadCreationMutex: failed
  validations come here from JIT code and the invalidation walks the
  thread map.
- STEAMAC_SMCSTATS=1: one "steamacsmc" line per second through
  __wine_dbg_output (faults, became hot, hot pages, validation misses,
  re-protects skipped, invalidations with and without code).
  0004's per-thread SMCSTAT is not ported (thread_local does not work
  in this module).

STEAMAC_SMC_HOT=0 turns all of the frontend changes off (old paths).

tools/smc-test (msfs2024-steamac), CrossOver 27 Preview runner copy:
T1 data writes into a code page 27-36 us -> 15-20 ns per iteration,
T6 512 pages 27-36 us -> 89 ns per call; T2-T4, T8 (protection
changes) and T7 (cross-thread patching in lock step, threads created
meanwhile) PASS with hot pages, with STEAMAC_SMC_HOT=0 and before.
tools/eh-test dr (20,001 x 4) and onlyskip (1000/1000), tools/dr-test
PASS, also with STEAMAC_SMC_HOT=0.

steamac local patch (msfs2024-steamac patches/fex). Not for upstream.
